<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 14_pseudo_elements/08: Tooltips from data attributes -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Tooltips from data attributes</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .tip { position: relative; border-bottom: 2px dotted #6366f1; cursor: help; }
    .tip::after { content: attr(data-tip); position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 130%; width: max-content; max-width: 16rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 6px; background: #1e1b4b; color: #fff; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.15s; pointer-events: none; }
    .tip:hover::after, .tip:focus::after { opacity: 1; }
    p { margin-top: 3rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Tooltips from data attributes</h1>
    <p class="lead">attr() reads the tip text from the element.</p>
    <p>Hover over <span class="tip" tabindex="0" data-tip="HyperText Markup Language">HTML</span> or
    <span class="tip" tabindex="0" data-tip="Cascading Style Sheets">CSS</span>.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
